    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "DNG Royal County are delighted to present 45 The Glebe, Maudlin Road, Kells, Co. Meath, a spacious three-bedroom semi-detached house for sale in the popular Glebe development in Kells.\n\n Extending to approximately 102 sq.m, this well-proportioned home presents an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, families or investors looking for a property within walking distance of Kells town centre. \n\nThe accommodation comprises a bright entrance hall, a comfortable living room with feature fireplace and a generous open-plan kitchen/dining area with patio doors opening onto the rear garden. A guest W.C. completes the ground-floor accommodation. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms, including a spacious master bedroom with en-suite shower room, together with a family bathroom. \n\nExternally, the property benefits from a driveway providing off-street parking, while the rear garden is laid mainly to lawn and includes a garden shed, offering plenty of scope to create an attractive outdoor space.\n\n\nThe Glebe is a popular and established residential development located on Maudlin Road in Kells, Co. Meath, within walking distance of Kells town centre and its excellent range of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, sporting facilities and local amenities.\n\nKells is a historic and well-connected town with convenient access to the M3 motorway, providing excellent connectivity to Navan, Dublin and the surrounding areas. The town is also well served by public transport, making it an attractive location for commuters.\n\nWith its spacious accommodation, off-street parking, rear garden and convenient location, 45 The Glebe represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a three-bedroom semi-detached home in one of Kells` established residential developments.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment with DNG Royal County."
      },
      {
